<section class="section">
    <div class="container content-grid">
        <div class="prose">
            <h2>Warranty coverage summary</h2>
            <div class="coverage-grid">
                <article class="coverage-card">
                    <strong>5 years*</strong>
                    <span>Manufacturer’s limited unit warranty</span>
                    <p>Coverage is provided by the manufacturer and remains subject to the written terms, exclusions, parts coverage and registration requirements for the exact unit and model.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="coverage-card">
                    <strong>2 years</strong>
                    <span>SAFE installation labor warranty</span>
                    <p>For 24 months from the installation date, SAFE covers qualifying correction of defects caused by SAFE’s original installation workmanship.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <p class="notice"><strong>Important:</strong> Online registration creates an organized SAFE warranty record. It does not expand, replace or change the manufacturer’s written warranty.</p>
            <h2>How a labor warranty request is reviewed</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>Contact SAFE and provide the warranty reference, property address and a description of the problem.</li>
                <li>A SAFE technician reviews the record and may request photos, troubleshooting information or an on-site inspection.</li>
                <li>The technician determines whether the issue resulted from SAFE’s original installation workmanship.</li>
                <li>If covered, SAFE will correct or reperform the affected installation work without a labor charge and will provide standard corrective materials related to that covered workmanship.</li>
            </ol>
            <h2>What is not automatically covered</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Manufacturer defects, failed internal parts or tank leaks controlled by the manufacturer’s warranty.</li>
                <li>Damage from abuse, neglect, freezing, flood, fire, power surge, hard water, corrosive water or external events.</li>
                <li>Changes or repairs made by another contractor, owner or third party after SAFE’s work.</li>
                <li>Existing plumbing, gas, electrical, venting, structural or code conditions not caused by SAFE.</li>
                <li>Maintenance, normal wear, cosmetic conditions or service outside the original installation scope.</li>
                <li>Permit, code-upgrade or access work that was not part of the original written scope.</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Inspection and authorization</h2>
            <p>A SAFE technician must inspect or otherwise verify the condition before coverage is approved. Do not authorize another company to alter the original installation before SAFE has a reasonable opportunity to inspect, except when immediate action is necessary to protect people or property.</p>
            <h2>Transfer and proof</h2>
            <p>The SAFE installation labor warranty remains associated with the original installed unit at the original property for the remainder of the 24-month term. Manufacturer transferability is governed only by the manufacturer’s terms. Keep the invoice, model and serial number, installation photos and warranty reference.</p>
        </div>
